# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-15: the second of three renames
on refactor/serialization-header-names, ahead of the serialization/
round's headers.

# Decided
- trueqbit asked whether serializing_util.h should become
  serializing_utils.h (plural); Claude leaned for streaming.h - every
  member streams SQL text into a std::ostream (stream_as, the
  streaming_* tags and their operator<<, stream_identifier,
  stream_sql_escaped), "streaming" reads in C++ as exactly that, and no
  other file of dev/ takes the name. trueqbit: "streaming.h (that's a
  good suggestion as the parent folder already carries
  `serialization`)". A grouping file: it takes an @file header.
- History read (git log --follow): 7476ea91 gathered it into
  serialization/, 2b038eab (note: the include of table_lookup.h it
  calls); the name predates both and carries no recorded reason.
- Pure rename: the file at 100% similarity; statement_serializer.h and
  execution/pragma.h, storage.h, storage_base.h, storage_definitions.h
  change their include line. clang-format sorts storage.h's include
  after statement_serializer.h, so the single header now reaches the
  file through the serializer: its 466 lines move from 22855 to 23165,
  still ahead of every use (first at 23420) and of
  statement_serializer (23681). The amalgamation holds the same lines,
  the include comments aside (checked as sorted multisets).
- Claude's report to trueqbit before the commits, "only the 8 include
  comment lines change", was read off a stale amalgamation (see 941a3e30's
  note: pre-commit.sh amalgamates before it formats); corrected in the
  report after this commit.

# Discussed
Green: pre-commit.sh 0 (run twice, the second on the formatted tree);
clang-format 20 unchanged; no "on purpose:". The token streams differ by
the include lines, as a rename makes them.

